#ifndef EWOK_STL_CINTTYPES_H
#define EWOK_STL_CINTTYPES_H

/*
 * <cinttypes> - the C <inttypes.h> names, in namespace std.
 *
 * This one is incomplete, and it is worth being precise about how and why
 * rather than papering over it.
 *
 * EwokOS's <inttypes.h> supplies the two greatest-width integer typedefs and
 * the whole PRI* / __EWOK_PRI64_PREFIX macro family - PRId8 through PRIX64 plus
 * the MAX variants - and that is what code almost always wants this header for,
 * since printf/scanf format strings for fixed-width types are otherwise
 * unportable between the 32-bit arm and 64-bit aarch64 targets this tree builds
 * for.  All of those are macros, so they need no using-declaration and are
 * available the moment the C header is included.
 *
 * What libc does NOT provide, and what is therefore absent from namespace std
 * here: imaxabs(), imaxdiv() and its imaxdiv_t result type, strtoimax(),
 * strtoumax(), wcstoimax() and wcstoumax().  [cinttypes.syn] requires all of
 * them.  They are left out on purpose instead of being implemented here:
 * arithmetic helpers for a type the C library is supposed to own belong in libc,
 * and defining them inside namespace std would put the STL in the business of
 * supplying libc functionality, which is exactly the layering the rest of these
 * <c*> wrappers are careful not to cross.  Nothing in QtCore, QtGui or QtWidgets
 * calls any of them.  If that changes, the fix is to add them to
 * system/basic/libc/libewoksys and then re-export them from here.
 */

#include <inttypes.h>

namespace std {

using ::intmax_t;
using ::uintmax_t;

}

#endif // EWOK_STL_CINTTYPES_H
